1
00:00:15,457 --> 00:00:17,199
"I'd like to sign up for The Next Leader."

2
00:00:17,199 --> 00:00:18,744
"On behalf of Ms. Tanya."

3
00:00:19,915 --> 00:00:20,848
Who's that kid?"

4
00:00:20,848 --> 00:00:22,377
"Are you referring to Din, sir?"

5
00:00:22,377 --> 00:00:23,953
"Please don't worry, sir."

6
00:00:23,953 --> 00:00:26,802
"There's no way Din can beat me."

7
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:29,098
"But with this one... I'm serious, you get me?"

8
00:00:29,098 --> 00:00:31,923
"I would like to welcome all the contestants of The Next Leader."

9
00:00:31,923 --> 00:00:33,311
"Good luck to you all."

10
00:00:33,311 --> 00:00:37,873
"The first challenge... locate three leaks in five minutes."

11
00:00:37,873 --> 00:00:42,102
"And the winning team is... Tanya's team!"

12
00:00:44,578 --> 00:00:45,503
"If my team wins...

13
00:00:45,503 --> 00:00:49,697
"the presidency must be mine."

14
00:00:57,660 --> 00:00:59,808
"Ah... the weather is so nice."

15
00:01:01,201 --> 00:01:02,976
"Then we'll fight together."

16
00:01:02,976 --> 00:01:04,461
"We'll win this together."

17
00:01:04,461 --> 00:01:05,242
"Yeah..."

18
00:01:05,242 --> 00:01:06,422
"You okay?"

19
00:01:06,422 --> 00:01:08,334
"Thank you."

20
00:01:36,030 --> 00:01:36,732
"Been waiting long?"

21
00:01:36,732 --> 00:01:38,784
"Took you forever!"

22
00:01:38,784 --> 00:01:42,202
"If I had to wait this long... why didn't you let me wait inside?"

23
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:44,851
"Calm down...

24
00:01:44,851 --> 00:01:47,794
if I let you up to my room right now, my dad will definitely find out."

25
00:01:49,236 --> 00:01:49,739
"Why?"

26
00:01:49,739 --> 00:01:52,323
"We're just friends. Is it wrong to wait in your room?"

27
00:01:56,069 --> 00:01:56,880
(Sighs) "If you want to be just friends..."

28
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:58,983
"you can be one by yourself."

29
00:01:58,983 --> 00:02:01,704
"Because I want to be more than that."

30
00:02:03,568 --> 00:02:05,086
"Wait, wait, wait...

31
00:02:05,086 --> 00:02:07,151
"what do you mean by that?"

32
00:02:09,692 --> 00:02:11,518
"What do you say... friend?"

33
00:02:13,483 --> 00:02:14,998
"I don't wanna be friends... I wanna be—"

34
00:02:18,316 --> 00:02:19,457
"Come on... we're gonna be late."

35
00:02:19,457 --> 00:02:25,259
"And besides... my dad's men might be around here... I'd be in trouble."

36
00:02:25,259 --> 00:02:25,982
KANGHAN: Really?
TIME: Yeah...

37
00:02:25,982 --> 00:02:28,309
TIME: Come on, hurry...
we're gonna be late for work.

38
00:02:28,309 --> 00:02:29,624
KANGHAN: Oh, right! Let's go, let's go!

39
00:02:29,624 --> 00:02:31,701
Please get in the car... Young Master Time.

40
00:02:31,701 --> 00:02:34,408
I told you... stop calling me Young Master Time.

41
00:02:36,772 --> 00:02:37,790
Just kidding.

42
00:02:39,855 --> 00:02:40,652
Oops... sorry. Sorry...

43
00:02:40,652 --> 00:02:42,211
Young Master.... sorry.

44
00:02:42,211 --> 00:02:43,663
It's fine... let's go

45
00:03:33,890 --> 00:03:34,957
KANGHAN:The weather is nice today, huh...KANGHAN: Yeah...

46
00:03:34,957 --> 00:03:37,375
TIME: It's not hot at all...KANGHAN: I'm hungry...

47
00:03:43,222 --> 00:03:43,962
"Good morning."

48
00:03:52,554 --> 00:03:53,915
"The second round is today, right?"

49
00:03:53,915 --> 00:03:55,715
"Yes, sir."

50
00:03:55,715 --> 00:03:58,252
"The competition begins at 1:00 PM."

51
00:03:59,470 --> 00:04:00,646
"We must win today...

52
00:04:00,646 --> 00:04:03,824
Did you take care of what I asked?"

53
00:04:04,886 --> 00:04:08,023
"Don't worry, sir... I will definitely win."

54
00:04:12,301 --> 00:04:12,987
"After you, sir."

55
00:04:39,256 --> 00:04:40,589
"Hey you...

56
00:04:40,589 --> 00:04:42,651
what's up? What are you doing?"

57
00:04:44,339 --> 00:04:45,708
"Just checking the equipment."

58
00:04:54,421 --> 00:04:55,387
"Alright, you're here..

59
00:04:55,387 --> 00:04:58,096
I'm counting on everyone today."

60
00:04:58,096 --> 00:05:01,623
"No problem... bro."

61
00:05:02,420 --> 00:05:04,213
"By the way... do you already have an idea of what we're going   to do?"

62
00:05:04,213 --> 00:05:06,627
"I have a few ideas in mind...

63
00:05:06,627 --> 00:05:08,113
but let's wait for today's brief first."

64
00:05:10,460 --> 00:05:12,527
"Hmm... speaking of the brief..."

65
00:05:12,527 --> 00:05:14,731
"Young Miss Ya...

66
00:05:14,731 --> 00:05:19,261
do you happen to have any inside scoop?"

67
00:05:19,261 --> 00:05:21,576
"What do you mean, brother?"

68
00:05:21,576 --> 00:05:25,607
"I was just talking nonsense... Here's the thing."

69
00:05:25,607 --> 00:05:28,771
"Ahem... the person giving us the brief... is the Chairman, right?"

70
00:05:28,771 --> 00:05:32,913
"So because of that... uh... between Young Miss Ya and the Chairman...

71
00:05:32,913 --> 00:05:36,526
did nothing leak out for us at all...?"

72
00:05:38,457 --> 00:05:42,092
"Well... I wish I knew. But this is my dad... he's my dad, you know?"

73
00:05:42,092 --> 00:05:45,257
"He barely even talks to me about the competition."

74
00:05:45,257 --> 00:05:47,515
"It's better that we find out at the same time...

75
00:05:48,706 --> 00:05:49,939
I don't want to cheat."

76
00:05:49,939 --> 00:05:51,063
"Fair is fair."

77
00:05:51,063 --> 00:05:53,427
"Yeah... I feel the same way."

78
00:05:53,427 --> 00:05:57,780
"But come to think of it... at least we know we're competing as a team today."

79
00:05:59,121 --> 00:06:02,730
"If that's the case... I'm gonna go check my gear. See you at the match."

80
00:06:02,730 --> 00:06:03,803
"Alright."

81
00:06:03,803 --> 00:06:04,633
"Let's go, Kanghan."

82
00:06:06,037 --> 00:06:06,671
"See ya!"

83
00:06:08,661 --> 00:06:12,059
"Those two hit it off pretty fast, didn't they?"

84
00:06:12,059 --> 00:06:14,119
"I'd better go check the gear too."

85
00:06:24,618 --> 00:06:25,581
"Great!"

86
00:07:31,776 --> 00:07:34,917
"Next up... here is the challenge for the second round."

87
00:07:34,917 --> 00:07:38,481
"...is the DIY pipe adaptation challenge...

88
00:07:38,481 --> 00:07:40,067
to present to the company."

89
00:07:40,067 --> 00:07:43,519
"Each team has three hours for production."

90
00:07:43,519 --> 00:07:44,879
"Ready...

91
00:07:44,879 --> 00:07:46,442
Begin!"

92
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:49,528
YA: "Woo! Let's do this!"
KANGHAN: "Let's go!"

93
00:07:50,523 --> 00:07:51,738
"Shoot."

94
00:07:51,738 --> 00:07:52,838
"So... what are we doing?"

95
00:07:52,838 --> 00:07:54,041
"Good question."

96
00:08:07,438 --> 00:08:09,326
"Guys... I've got an idea."

97
00:08:09,326 --> 00:08:12,565
"Whoa! That was fast. Thought this was MasterChef... what's on the menu?"

98
00:08:12,565 --> 00:08:13,732
"Be serious."

99
00:08:13,732 --> 00:08:17,021
"So, what's your concept, Din?"

100
00:08:17,021 --> 00:08:18,203
"Exactly."

101
00:08:21,394 --> 00:08:22,725
"We're going to build an electric bike."

102
00:08:22,725 --> 00:08:24,214
"An electric bike?!"

103
00:08:25,685 --> 00:08:27,109
"Whoa! That's awesome!"

104
00:08:27,109 --> 00:08:28,514
"How do you even ride it? .

105
00:08:28,514 --> 00:08:30,399
..Let me test it out."

106
00:08:30,399 --> 00:08:33,226
"Alright, come on! Let's get to work!"

107
00:08:49,432 --> 00:08:52,047
"Alright... it's time to inspect your work."

108
00:08:52,047 --> 00:08:53,602
"Let's start with Team A."

109
00:08:53,602 --> 00:08:56,942
"Din, please present your project."

110
00:09:07,430 --> 00:09:10,930
[Team A: Electric Bike]

111
00:09:10,930 --> 00:09:14,978
"Our project focuses on simplicity and practicality.

112
00:09:14,978 --> 00:09:19,548
The locals can easily repair it themselves, and the materials are widely available."

113
00:09:19,548 --> 00:09:22,666
"Practical... are you sure about that?"

114
00:09:26,178 --> 00:09:30,079
"Next up, Team B. Pong, the floor is yours."

115
00:09:30,079 --> 00:09:32,568
"Alright... let's go!"

116
00:09:36,468 --> 00:09:38,957
[Team B: Electric 4-Wheeler]

117
00:09:38,957 --> 00:09:43,200
"Well, we built a renewable energy vehicle."

118
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:50,826
"We use fuel derived from waste plastic through pyrolysis... to reduce waste........"

119
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:53,603
"Why does their idea sound exactly like ours?"

120
00:09:53,603 --> 00:09:55,108
"Damn it... did they cheat?"

121
00:09:55,108 --> 00:09:55,678
"Yeah..."

122
00:10:02,590 --> 00:10:06,194
"In the real world... simplicity doesn't cut it."

123
00:10:06,194 --> 00:10:10,229
"They look at results... that generate value."

124
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:15,027
"Someone like you will never have what it takes to lead anyone."

125
00:10:17,004 --> 00:10:19,681
"Ahem! But a cheater... could never lead anyone either."

126
00:10:19,681 --> 00:10:23,749
"Hey! What... Who? Sounds like a sore loser to me."

127
00:10:37,502 --> 00:10:38,003
"Alright...

128
00:10:38,003 --> 00:10:41,972
regarding the challenge of applying DIY pipes for the corporate pitch..."

129
00:10:41,972 --> 00:10:50,405
"The judges have evaluated based on cost, creativity... and most importantly, commercial viability."

130
00:10:50,405 --> 00:10:53,647
"And the winning team is..."

131
00:10:57,874 --> 00:10:58,911
"Team B... Mr. Pong."

132
00:10:58,911 --> 00:11:01,849
"Yeah!"

133
00:11:01,849 --> 00:11:04,125
"Yeah! ...How do you like that, huh?"

134
00:11:12,122 --> 00:11:13,030
"Mr. Din...

135
00:11:15,580 --> 00:11:16,613
how about a handshake?"

136
00:11:24,037 --> 00:11:27,483
"Last time... was just a fluke."

137
00:11:27,483 --> 00:11:32,134
"Let's face it... someone like you could never beat me."

138
00:11:35,036 --> 00:11:35,659
"Let's go."

139
00:11:45,618 --> 00:11:46,576
"Damn it... they cheated."

140
00:11:46,576 --> 00:11:49,266
"Obviously... they even used the exact same pipe specs."

141
00:11:49,266 --> 00:11:49,766
"Right!"

142
00:11:51,326 --> 00:11:52,417
"It's okay, Din."

143
00:12:02,616 --> 00:12:03,659
"I'm so fucking pissed."

144
00:12:03,659 --> 00:12:05,704
"Damn... are they seriously just judging by the surface?"

145
00:12:05,704 --> 00:12:11,623
"True... but honestly, their car is really impressive given the time limit."

146
00:12:11,623 --> 00:12:16,453
"P'Ya! The theme was DIY. How the hell is that DIY?"

147
00:12:16,453 --> 00:12:20,416
"Damn... you're right. Should we just protest to the judges?"

148
00:12:20,416 --> 00:12:23,544
"Let it go... a loss is a loss."

149
00:12:23,544 --> 00:12:25,631
"At the very least... we have to accept the decision."

150
00:12:25,631 --> 00:12:31,859
"No... but seriously, what kind of judging was that? Pong might have bribed the judges."

151
00:12:31,859 --> 00:12:34,396
"He'd do absolutely anything to win."

152
00:12:34,396 --> 00:12:39,423
"Yeah, I agree... Actually, there's one thing I'm suspicious about."

153
00:12:39,423 --> 00:12:44,890
"Why the hell did their PVC e-bike prototype... turn out exactly like ours?"

154
00:12:44,890 --> 00:12:51,224
"Even the pipe sizes are identical... It's like they knew exactly what we were planning."

155
00:12:52,026 --> 00:12:52,668
YA : "You're actually right."

156
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:03,000
"Listen... there's one more thing."

157
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:07,264
"The prototype P'Din drew over there... only the four of us knew about it."

158
00:13:07,264 --> 00:13:10,534
"Kanghan... don't suspect our own people."

159
00:13:10,534 --> 00:13:14,085
"P'Din... I'm not doubting us...

160
00:13:14,085 --> 00:13:16,673
but you have to admit, it's weird."

161
00:13:19,189 --> 00:13:20,375
"P'Pong isn't actually that good...

162
00:13:20,375 --> 00:13:24,805
he just knows exactly what to steal."

163
00:13:24,805 --> 00:13:27,769
"Time... what do you mean? Do you know something?"

164
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:34,248
"Right! That bastard Pong must have sent someone to steal our prototype."

165
00:13:34,248 --> 00:13:40,699
"That's true... he might have sent someone to spy on us... because we let our guard down during our meetings."

166
00:13:40,699 --> 00:13:46,271
"Yeah... we really didn't watch our backs this round. We let our guard down."

167
00:13:46,271 --> 00:13:51,033
"It didn't even cross our minds. The stakes were damn high... sigh."

168
00:13:53,643 --> 00:13:54,792
"P'Din, P'Ya...

169
00:13:57,268 --> 00:14:00,344
I'm tired. Let's just call it a day."

170
00:14:00,344 --> 00:14:04,370
"Yeah, you're right. Let's call it a day. Thank you all so much...

171
00:14:04,370 --> 00:14:06,011
Thanks, Ya."

172
00:14:10,599 --> 00:14:11,440
"I'm gonna head out first, P'Din."

173
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:13,500
"See ya."

174
00:14:16,432 --> 00:14:19,211
(Ya sighs heavily)
DIN: Hey... it's alright.

175
00:14:23,889 --> 00:14:28,896
"This guy Din's work... it's deceptively simple, yet remarkably clever."

176
00:14:31,888 --> 00:14:34,554
"Dad... let me ask you something straight."

177
00:14:34,554 --> 00:14:37,188
"Why do you have to get in their way?"

178
00:14:38,554 --> 00:14:39,801
"The stakes are too high."

179
00:14:39,801 --> 00:14:41,823
"I only care about winning."

180
00:14:44,137 --> 00:14:47,511
"Thanks a lot for the insider info, Time."

181
00:14:50,052 --> 00:14:53,517
"I did everything you asked... I gave the designs to P'Pong."

182
00:14:53,517 --> 00:14:55,364
"Are you happy now, Dad?"

183
00:14:55,364 --> 00:15:00,957
"Please... I'm begging you. Just stop making me hurt other people."

184
00:15:00,957 --> 00:15:03,093
"This is just the beginning.

185
00:15:03,093 --> 00:15:07,356
For Din's next project... I'll need your help again."

186
00:15:08,967 --> 00:15:10,133
"He has to lose."

187
00:15:12,383 --> 00:15:13,774
"I'm gonna have to count on you again, Time."

188
00:15:16,007 --> 00:15:16,894
"That's enough!"

189
00:15:16,894 --> 00:15:21,482
"Go back to them... and act like nothing happened."

190
00:15:21,482 --> 00:15:23,838
"Now get out."

191
00:15:23,838 --> 00:15:26,134
"Yes... Dad."

192
00:15:31,047 --> 00:15:35,267
"Do you think... Time might soften up and tell them everything, sir?"

193
00:15:37,046 --> 00:15:38,648
"Someday, Time will understand...

194
00:15:38,648 --> 00:15:42,314
why I had to do what I did."

195
00:15:43,379 --> 00:15:43,997
"As for you...

196
00:15:43,997 --> 00:15:46,913
keep a close eye on Time."

197
00:15:46,913 --> 00:15:50,869
"Don't let him grow a soft spot and ruin everything."

198
00:15:52,211 --> 00:15:53,367
"Consider it done, sir."

199
00:16:34,122 --> 00:16:35,497
"Here."

200
00:16:35,497 --> 00:16:37,464
"Thought you might want something warm to drink."

201
00:16:40,455 --> 00:16:42,518
"I saw you chewing on that ice until it completely melted."

202
00:16:49,870 --> 00:16:50,613
Thank you.

203
00:17:03,202 --> 00:17:06,549
"Why have you looked so stressed all day?"

204
00:17:06,549 --> 00:17:09,494
"I didn't even dare to talk to you."

205
00:17:12,326 --> 00:17:16,989
"Still upset about today's loss?"

206
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:23,666
"Yeah... a little bit."

207
00:17:31,782 --> 00:17:32,448
"P'Time..."

208
00:17:32,448 --> 00:17:33,500
"Hmm?"

209
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:37,929
"I know you're Mr. Perfect...

210
00:17:37,929 --> 00:17:41,754
and you probably hate losing."

211
00:17:44,197 --> 00:17:48,928
"But I really don't like seeing you like this."

212
00:18:21,109 --> 00:18:23,273
"How's that? Feeling any better?"

213
00:18:27,774 --> 00:18:30,965
"If this doesn't work, I don't know what will."

214
00:18:32,940 --> 00:18:34,959
"So, how do you think you should comfort me?"

215
00:18:43,772 --> 00:18:44,508
"Here you go."

216
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:47,897
"Ta-da!

217
00:18:47,897 --> 00:18:48,259
Hmm?"

218
00:18:48,259 --> 00:18:49,922
"What is this?"

219
00:18:49,922 --> 00:18:51,737
"Coloring."

220
00:18:51,737 --> 00:18:54,036
"Coloring?"

221
00:18:54,036 --> 00:18:56,890
"Yeah... whenever I'm stressed, I like to color."

222
00:18:56,890 --> 00:18:59,667
"It really helps... give it a try."

223
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:06,965
"Here, spread out a few pages."

224
00:19:06,965 --> 00:19:11,410
"I love doing this. It really helps relieve stress."

225
00:19:11,410 --> 00:19:13,768
"Really? Show me first."

226
00:19:17,185 --> 00:19:20,020
"I like to just draw... whatever comes to mind."

227
00:19:22,017 --> 00:19:22,719
"Let's see it, then."

228
00:19:22,719 --> 00:19:23,775
"Like this."

229
00:19:23,775 --> 00:19:24,916
"What is that supposed to be?"

230
00:19:24,916 --> 00:19:27,480
"It reflects how we feel."

231
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,235
"It's terrible."

232
00:20:36,216 --> 00:20:39,278
"It's getting late... and you're still buried in all this metal."

233
00:20:39,278 --> 00:20:42,994
"This won't make the bad feelings go away, you know."

234
00:20:45,548 --> 00:20:46,716
"I don't want to rest."

235
00:20:46,716 --> 00:20:50,990
"Whenever I close my eyes, today's mistakes just keep replaying in my head."

236
00:20:50,990 --> 00:20:56,710
"Din... everyone makes mistakes.

237
00:20:56,710 --> 00:20:59,830
You did your best today."

238
00:21:03,921 --> 00:21:06,544
"But if I had been just a little more careful today...

239
00:21:06,544 --> 00:21:09,501
our team wouldn't have lost. It's all my fault."

240
00:21:11,087 --> 00:21:16,789
"Listen... if anyone is to blame, it should be me. I was barely any help to anyone."

241
00:21:16,789 --> 00:21:18,410
"I just made things harder for you."

242
00:21:40,291 --> 00:21:43,051
"Look... I really struggled using this today."

243
00:21:43,051 --> 00:21:45,041
"Could you show me how?"

244
00:21:45,041 --> 00:21:46,567
"Please?"

245
00:21:46,567 --> 00:21:48,797
"But it's dangerous... it's not a toy, you know."

246
00:21:48,797 --> 00:21:51,258
"That's exactly why I need you to teach me."

247
00:21:51,258 --> 00:21:55,450
"It's good for me to pick up these skills anyway..."

248
00:21:55,450 --> 00:22:00,480
"...so I can actually help you out. Please? Teach me."

249
00:22:00,480 --> 00:22:03,095
"You're so stubborn."

250
00:22:03,095 --> 00:22:05,835
"Okay...

251
00:22:05,835 --> 00:22:12,392
but you have to follow every step." "No arguing... and absolutely do not let go. Understood?"

252
00:22:12,392 --> 00:22:13,884
"Understood, boss."

253
00:22:15,745 --> 00:22:18,135
"First things first... you need to put on gloves."

254
00:22:21,744 --> 00:22:22,538
"Here... give me your hand."

255
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:29,398
"Is this just an excuse to hold my hand?"

256
00:22:29,398 --> 00:22:31,194
"Safety first."

257
00:22:33,243 --> 00:22:34,534
"How's that?

258
00:22:38,867 --> 00:22:40,554
"Alright... let me go grab the tools."

259
00:22:40,554 --> 00:22:44,037
"...the pipe fittings."

260
00:22:44,037 --> 00:22:47,594
"Here...

261
00:22:47,594 --> 00:22:50,165
hold onto this."

262
00:22:50,165 --> 00:22:53,653
"Okay... spread your feet a little."

263
00:22:53,653 --> 00:22:56,747
"Okay...Hold it tight right here."

264
00:23:04,864 --> 00:23:05,467
"Are you ready?"

265
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:08,002
"I'm ready."

266
00:23:08,002 --> 00:23:14,490
"First, we mark the spot... hold the pipe tight."

267
00:23:14,490 --> 00:23:15,081
Din: "Got a good grip?"
Ya: "Got it."

268
00:23:15,081 --> 00:23:22,870
"Wow... we could be cutting this all day and it still wouldn't go through."

269
00:23:22,870 --> 00:23:27,168
"Here... let me show you."

270
00:23:27,168 --> 00:23:35,313
"You have to hold the pipe tight. See? We want to cut right here. So, we place it down."

271
00:23:35,313 --> 00:23:39,098
"And apply steady pressure..."

272
00:23:39,098 --> 00:23:41,609
"Din!!"

273
00:23:41,609 --> 00:23:45,275
"Hey... how are you holding up?"

274
00:23:45,275 --> 00:23:47,384
Ya: "I'm so sorry."
Din: "It's nothing. I'm fine."

275
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:48,864
"Let's get that cleaned up first."

276
00:23:48,864 --> 00:23:52,642
"I'm so sorry."

277
00:23:52,642 --> 00:23:54,013
"It's nothing. I'm fine."

278
00:23:54,013 --> 00:23:55,400
"Let's get that cleaned up first."

279
00:24:10,939 --> 00:24:13,553
[1 Day Earlier]

280
00:24:44,601 --> 00:24:45,925
"Working hard this early, huh?

281
00:24:48,100 --> 00:24:48,920
Have you eaten anything yet?

282
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:52,527
"I don't usually eat breakfast."

283
00:24:57,099 --> 00:24:58,016
"Here, I got you some coffee."

284
00:24:58,016 --> 00:25:00,204
"Thank you."

285
00:25:00,204 --> 00:25:03,594
"Are you working on this afternoon's presentation? I saw you doing that since yesterday."

286
00:25:03,594 --> 00:25:10,324
"Yeah. It's P'Jum. She suddenly wanted to add a bunch of stuff. I'm barely going to finish in time."

287
00:25:48,551 --> 00:25:49,089
"Hey, idiot...

288
00:25:49,089 --> 00:25:51,050
you here already?"

289
00:25:51,050 --> 00:25:57,126
"Why aren't you coming in, then?

290
00:25:57,126 --> 00:25:57,626
..Huh?! ...Why the hell are you over there?

291
00:25:57,626 --> 00:26:00,755
You're at the wrong place. ...Unbelievable."

292
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:09,548
"Oh, come on!"

293
00:26:09,548 --> 00:26:11,238
"Hey!"

294
00:26:11,238 --> 00:26:12,899
Din: "Hey!"
Yha: "Whoa!"

295
00:26:12,899 --> 00:26:14,572
Yha: "Din...!"
Din: "What?!"

296
00:26:14,572 --> 00:26:18,043
"I didn't save my file yet!"

297
00:26:18,043 --> 00:26:20,773
"Here, let me take a look."

298
00:26:20,773 --> 00:26:24,755
"Hey... oh no, what do I do?!"

299
00:26:24,755 --> 00:26:26,024
"Ugh... it's too late."

300
00:26:32,004 --> 00:26:34,547
"Good thing you worked on Canva. It saves automatically."

301
00:26:34,547 --> 00:26:42,115
"Phew... true. I totally forgot. If I didn't have anything to submit, P'Jum would've ripped my head off."

302
00:26:48,502 --> 00:26:49,199
"Pervert!"

303
00:26:49,199 --> 00:26:52,300
"I'm sorry, I didn't mean to."

304
00:26:52,300 --> 00:26:56,367
"You're so sensitive... Just like the other day with your skirt."

305
00:26:56,367 --> 00:26:58,845
"And it always has to be you!"

306
00:27:00,875 --> 00:27:02,583
"Get out of here... I'll finish this myself."

307
00:27:02,583 --> 00:27:03,992
"Thank you."

308
00:27:20,956 --> 00:27:22,331
Whoa, whoa, whoa!"

309
00:27:22,331 --> 00:27:23,293
"What?!"

310
00:27:23,293 --> 00:27:25,899
Ya: "The computer, the computer!"
Din: "What is it?!"

311
00:27:25,899 --> 00:27:29,972
"It saves automatically."

312
00:27:29,972 --> 00:27:31,735
"It crashed!"

313
00:27:31,735 --> 00:27:32,235
"What?!"

314
00:27:32,235 --> 00:27:35,109
"Move, let me look, Whoa..."

315
00:27:35,109 --> 00:27:38,921
I can't take this anymore."

316
00:27:38,921 --> 00:27:44,743
Yha: "Come on, hurry! We're out of time!"
Din: "Okay, I'm going as fast as I can for you."

317
00:27:44,743 --> 00:27:47,965
Yha: "This is impossible!"
Din: "I'm trying my best here."

318
00:27:47,965 --> 00:27:50,596
Din: "I have no idea what's wrong with your computer."

319
00:27:50,596 --> 00:27:54,118
Yha: "Oh god, what are we going to do?! ...Come on, you can do it!"

320
00:27:54,118 --> 00:27:55,333
Din: "I'm trying my best!"

321
00:28:15,990 --> 00:28:18,122
"Bro... do you think he knows it was us?"

322
00:28:20,698 --> 00:28:21,617
"Is she going to be mad at us?"

323
00:28:52,486 --> 00:28:58,075
"However, if you choose surgery, there will be out-of-pocket expenses of about 500,000 baht that cannot be reimbursed."

324
00:29:06,275 --> 00:29:07,200
Kangkhan: "It's going to be okay."

325
00:29:07,200 --> 00:29:12,474
Pong: "If you agree, that mere 500,000 baht... I can just pay it for you."

326
00:29:16,108 --> 00:29:17,878
Din: "What did you just say?"
Pong: "Whoa, whoa, whoa!"

327
00:29:17,878 --> 00:29:19,680
Pong: "Didn't he tell you...

328
00:29:19,680 --> 00:29:22,611
that he came to me for help?"

329
00:29:22,611 --> 00:29:27,464
Pong: "In exchange for withdrawing from the final round."

330
00:29:28,314 --> 00:29:31,609
"And don't act suspicious... don't let them know we set this up."

331
00:29:31,609 --> 00:29:34,947
"Don't you feel sorry for P'Din and P'Yha...? All of us put so much dedication into..."

332
00:29:34,947 --> 00:29:36,619
"Do you think I wanted to do this?!"
